Gamma is a solid modeling compiler.  It can translate programs written
in Scheme or Lua into geometry that is numerically robust and free of
defects.  Gamma supports a wide range of techniques, including CSG
modeling, generalized 2D to 3D extrusion, subdivision methods, surface
fairing and deformation.

Gamma is intended for programmers who wish to apply their skills to
the design of physical objects, but it may also appeal to designers
used to interactive tools.  It is particularly suitable for parametric
models, or those best described in mathematical terms.

Gamma can be invoked on the command line like a compiler, or through
its companion, Gamma Debugger, for an interactive graphical interface.
